tains of Washington, U.S.. It is located in Olympic National Park, and is a high point on the High Divide separating the Hoh River and Sol Duc River valleys, and forming the southern rim of Seven Lakes Basin. The peak is situated at the headwaters of the Bogachiel River. The name \"Bogachiel\" is a corruption of the Quileute words bo qwa tcheel el, or /boqʷač'íʔl/, from /bó:q'ʷa/, \"muddy\", and /číʔlowa/, \"water\", meaning \"gets riley [turbid] after a rain\", \"muddy waters\", or, less likely, \"big river\".","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bogachiel_Peak","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Mount_Olympus_-_panoramio_-_FishSpeaker.jpg/960px-Mount_Olympus_-_panoramio_-_FishSpeaker.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Olympus_-_panoramio_-_FishSpeaker.jpg","dist_m":7,"width":640,"height":296,"license":"CC BY 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","artist":"FishSpeaker"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Mount_Olympus_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-Mount_Olympus_-_panoramio.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Olympus_-_panoramio.jpg","dist_m":7,"width":640,"height":449,"license":"CC BY 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","artist":"FishSpeaker"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Seven_Lakes_Basin_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-Seven_Lakes_Basin_-_panoramio.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seven_Lakes_Basin_-_panoramio.jpg","dist_m":297,"width":640,"height":428,"license":"CC BY 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","artist":"FishSpeaker"}],"street":null},{"id":"node/356544818","name":"Eagle Point","kind":"peak","lon":-123.40905,"lat":47.93917,"ele_m":1904.1,"wikidata":"Q49026677","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle_Point_(Olympic_Mountains)"},{"id":"node/348997349","name":"Hur